10600	{"artifactId":"LLD-670419c4ad8bea8e-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-670419c4ad8bea8e-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-17T12:44:39.150Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers S001's durable personal history, unchanged delivery state, and restart recovery requirements.","evidence":"DEF S001/ac1 requires answers, confidence, assisted attempts and progress to remain associated with the original change; ac2 preserves delivery status and approvals; ac3 requires recovery without accidental pass. The proposed immutable scope, separate history namespaces, atomic writes, interrupted-job recovery and unavailable eligibility address these requirements. [files: docs/epics/understand-changes-before-committing-E20261017670419c4/DEF.md, src/db/graph/store.ts]","action":"Preserve these invariants during implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Identity precedence and retention until explicit deletion reflect the resolved upstream decisions.","evidence":"HLD metadata specifies one connected provider identity, repository-configured Git email when multiple identities exist, OS fallback, and distinct identities unless explicitly linked. Its retention resolution says: 'Retain the learner's assessment history locally until that learner explicitly deletes it' with private history, sharing disabled and no automatic expiry. The design preserves these decisions. [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-670419c4ad8bea8e.json]","action":"Keep these resolutions as acceptance fixtures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"GraphStore currently opens 27 named databases with MAX_DBS set to 32.","evidence":"Reading the complete store construction yields 27 named database opens, ending with exploration_cache. The constant is 'const MAX_DBS = 32'. Adding eight namespaces yields 35, so increasing capacity is necessary. [files: src/db/graph/store.ts]","action":"Implement the proposed capacity increase and inventory assertion together.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing streaming transport substitutes request IDs, uses a void send callback, and does not automatically emit done.","evidence":"StreamHandler accepts 'send: (msg: IpcStreamMessage) => void'. handleStreamMessage constructs '{ ...msg, id: request.id }', awaits the handler, and only removes listeners afterward; it emits an error on an uncaught handler failure but no automatic done. IpcStreamKind already includes progress, done and error. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/shared/types.ts]","action":"Retain the proposed explicit terminal frames and domain events inside progress.data.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"withWriteTxn supports the proposed atomic multi-namespace mutation with a synchronous callback.","evidence":"The complete implementation obtains GraphStore, executes store.root.childTransaction(run), rejects thenable callback results, awaits transaction settlement and detects lock loss. Its documented child-transaction behavior rolls back a throwing callback without rolling back neighboring callers. [files: src/db/graph/store.ts]","action":"Await withWriteTxn before acknowledgment and keep all callback work synchronous.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The role taxonomy and floor guard are reusable, while the five understanding role descriptors are new.","evidence":"The complete ROLES registry contains no understanding roles. RoleDescriptor exposes id, criticality and defaultTier; roleDescriptor returns undefined for absent entries. applyCoreFloor clamps critical roles against the configured floor. The proposed registration and explicit missing-descriptor check fit these APIs. [files: src/config/role-taxonomy.ts, src/config/core-floor-guard.ts]","action":"Test both descriptor registration and configured-floor behavior; critical does not independently force core under every configuration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design identifies the existing transport and lifecycle integration sites needed for command registration and bounded shutdown flushing.","evidence":"daemon/index.ts constructs IpcServer from separate RPC and stream handler registries. Its stopBackgroundWork initiates server.close without awaiting it; closeStores runs after queue drain. server.ts writes directly without tracking write callbacks. These are the sites the design proposes extending, without changing the public send callback. [files: src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts]","action":"Cover both ordinary response writes and stream writes in pending-write tracking.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing connection metadata provides a concrete integration path for enumerating authenticated GitHub, GitLab and Jira stable subjects.","evidence":"The analyzer failed during planning with shaper-llm-unavailable caused by an invalid response schema. Subsequent source searches and reads found GitHub tracker configuration and ghAuthOk(), which runs 'gh auth status' and returns only ok/reason. Repository owner/repo metadata is not authenticated learner identity. No concrete stable-subject enumeration API or GitLab/Jira connection adapter was identified. [files: src/workflow/config/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Specify each adapter's module, metadata source, stable-ID field and unavailable behavior. Distinguish a missing integration from an available authenticated identity that the implementation must discover.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Assessment versioning should be separate from graph versioning, with additive namespaces rather than a graph schema rewrite.","evidence":"GraphStore currently uses SCHEMA_VERSION = 5 and stores its version in meta under schema_version. Its initialization dispatches graph migrations from that value. The inspected namespace inventory and source searches contain no existing assessment storage format. A separate understanding_meta/version boundary avoids misinterpreting graph versions as assessment versions. [files: src/db/graph/store.ts, docs/epics/understand-changes-before-committing-E20261017670419c4/HLD.md]","action":"Keep assessment initialization and unsupported-version handling separate from existing graph migration logic, as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design preserves the HLD's shared contracts and defers grading, editor behavior, Git capture and overrides to their owning stories.","evidence":"HLD sc1 contains the scope fields retained by the canonical tuple, including commitMode and ordered parentOids. sc2 contains the same AssessmentService sketch. sc4 defines confidence as unsure/low/medium/high. HLD §6 assigns foundational schemas and role registration to s1, grading to s3, editor integration to s5, capture/enforcement to s6 and exceptions to s7. The LLD follows those boundaries. [files: docs/epics/understand-changes-before-committing-E20261017670419c4/HLD.md]","action":"Keep sibling implementations behind the proposed validated internal registration boundary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed shutdown handling can preserve the existing forced-exit and lock-loss behavior.","evidence":"createShutdown is re-entrant guarded, invokes stopBackgroundWork synchronously, defaults hardExitMs to 20,000, and bypasses queue/store closure after detected lock loss in favor of SIGKILL. The proposed flush is confined to healthy closeStores and bounded to 1,000ms, so it need not replace these paths. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"Keep stop hooks free of database waits and retain the proposed forced-exit, disconnect and re-entrant tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each S001 acceptance criterion has a corresponding proposed test using compatible repository test infrastructure.","evidence":"DEF ac1 maps to persistence/reopen and identity/scope tests; ac2 maps to unchanged delivery-artifact assertions; ac3 maps to interrupted-job recovery, rollback and reconnect tests. Existing graph tests use node:test, node:assert/strict, temporary directories, setGraphStorePath and closeGraphStore, supporting the proposed isolated persistence suite. Existing server registry tests use fake sockets, so the promised real-socket shutdown tests are additional work, not existing coverage. [files: docs/epics/understand-changes-before-committing-E20261017670419c4/DEF.md, src/db/graph/__tests__/store.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/server-registry.test.ts]","action":"Implement the mapped tests, explicitly including failed and skipped assessment transitions for ac2. This review did not execute tests or verify future implementation behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":12,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-17T12:44:39.150Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
